course: dictionary
lesson: 7791
title: Quake: shaking ground and shaking knees
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quake is a short way of saying earthquake: the ground suddenly shakes because rocks deep underground move. Read the words around it to be sure. «Nobody can yet say on which day an earthquake will strike, but scientists can map where the risk is high and how strong the quakes there can be.» Here the quakes are shakes of the ground, because they are strong and they strike a place.
explain: To quake can also be a verb, and then it means to shake or tremble. People often quake because they are very scared or very cold. «Swarms of small quakes» means many tiny shakes close together, and the sentence goes on to say they can warn people to move away.
explain: Stories use quake for fear. «Quake with fear» and «quake in your boots» tell you a character is terrified, even if nothing is shaking at all. Your clues are the rest of the sentence: a scared face, a locked door, a creaking step. When you swap in "shake" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: A quake is a short word for an earthquake.
fact: An earthquake happens when rocks deep under the ground suddenly move.
fact: To quake means to shake or tremble, often from fear or cold.
fact: «Quake with fear» and «quake in your boots» mean a person is terrified.
fact: Scientists cannot yet say the exact day an earthquake will strike, but they can map where the risk is high.
exercise: «Scientists can map where the risk is high and how strong the quakes there can be.» What are the quakes in this sentence? | Loud bangs from fireworks | *Earthquakes, when the ground suddenly shakes | Holes dug for building | Storms that bring heavy rain
exercise: «Tom began to quake in his boots as the door creaked open.» What does quake mean here? | Fall fast asleep | Jump with joy | Sing loudly | *Shake with fear
exercise: «Volcanologists watch for swarms of small quakes before they warn people to move away.» What do the small quakes give? | Sweet and sticky treats | Good weather for the weekend | A sale at the shops | *A warning that the ground may be moving
test:
«Her knees began to quake as she stood on the stage.» What does quake mean here? | Stay still and calm | *Shake because she is scared | Grow taller very quickly | Sleep soundly
Which word is a short way of saying earthquake? | Quilt | *Quake | Quarry | Quiet
exam:
Which sentence uses quake to mean shake because of cold? | The sun was hot and the sand was warm | *He was so cold that his teeth began to quake | She read a long book at the library | The dog ran across the park to fetch a ball
